==English==

===Etymology===
Coined 1989 by Julie Connelly in a Fortune magazine cover story, by analogy with a real estate ''trophy building.''<ref>{{cite-web
|title=The CEO’s Second Wife
|author=Julie Connelly
|work=Fortune Magazine
|date=August 28, 1989
|url=http://money.cnn.com/magazines/fortune/fortune_archive/1989/08/28/72407/index.htm
|passage=Powerful men are beginning to demand '''trophy wives.''' {{...}} The more money men make, the argument goes, the more self-assured they become, and the easier it is for them to think: I deserve a queen.
}}</ref><ref>{{cite-web
|title=ON LANGUAGE; Trophy Wife
|date=1994-05-01
|work=The New York Times
|author=William Safire
|authorlink=William Safire
|url=http://query.nytimes.com/gst/fullpage.html?res=9F06E6DA1031F932A35756C0A962958260&sec=&spon=&pagewanted=all}}</ref>

===Noun===
{{en-noun|trophy wives}}

# {{lb|en|derogatory}} A wife, usually [[young]] and [[attractive]], regarded as a [[status symbol]] for the [[husband]], usually [[older]] and [[affluent]].
#* {{quote-book
|en
|year=1991
|chapter=It Can't Last
|title=Generation X
|author=Douglas Coupland
|authorlink=Douglas Coupland
|passage={{...}} while Mrs. Scott-Baxter, his fourth (and '''trophy) wife''', blonde and young and bored, glowered at the Baxter spawn like a mother mink in a mink farm, just waiting for a jet to strafe the facility, affording her an excuse to feign terror and eat her young.}}
#* '''2008''', Julia Llewellyn, ''The Model Wife'', Penguin UK ({{ISBN|9780141911564}})
#*: ‘She's with her nanny.’ ‘Oh yeah, I forgot. You're a proper '''trophy wife''' now. Staff and everything. Well…’ She produced a bottle of cava from a plastic bag. ‘With no child to keep up appearances for, let's get  ourselves in the mood.’
#* '''2013''', George G. Nyman, ''Love Lost in Time Relativity'', AuthorHouse ({{ISBN|9781491834039}}), page 12:
#*: She was David's fourth wife. Twenty-four years his junior, they both knew why they were together. David was filthy rich, and Belinda was a '''trophy wife'''. In fact, this was her third time around in this career: Being a '''trophy wife'''.

